The order‑processing platform is deliberately split into a set of loosely coupled micro‑services that communicate via an event‑driven backbone (Apache Kafka) while exposing a RESTful façade through an API Gateway. The core services are implemented in Spring Boot, leverage Axon for Command Query Responsibility Segregation (CQRS) and Event Sourcing (ES), and use Resilience4j to enforce fault‑tolerance guarantees. The following sections walk through the data‑flow, resilience strategies, observability stack, and compliance safeguards that collectively satisfy the success criteria outlined earlier.

### 1. Data‑flow and Service Interaction

